# WorkforceGuard AI

Read `CLAUDE.md` and `CONTRIBUTING.md` for the canonical workflow. This rule mirrors them for Cursor.

## Git (required)

- Never commit or push to `main`. Branch first: `feature/…`, `fix/…`, `chore/…`
- Ship via PR; CI must pass before merge
- Do not use `git commit --no-verify` unless the user explicitly requests it
- One branch per task; focused diffs only

## Verify before done

| Changed | Run |
|---------|-----|
| `dashboard/frontend/` | `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm test` |
| `dashboard/backend/` | `pytest dashboard/backend/tests/ -q` (needs `DATABASE_URL` for auth) |
| `scripts/` or root `tests/` | `pytest tests/ -q` |
| `analytics/` | `dbt test` (not in CI yet) |

## Never commit

`.env`, secrets, `data/internal/`, `data/tenants/`, raw video under `docs/demos/video_recording/`

## Layout

- `dashboard/frontend/` — React UI
- `dashboard/backend/` — FastAPI + auth
- `analytics/` — dbt models
- `scripts/` — data pipelines
- `deploy/` — GCP/Vercel

Match existing code style. Add tests when behavior changes. User also uses Claude Code — commit/stash before switching tools on a branch.
